{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qT1LpmKBS2c7NR17dneAf","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"papers:\\\\n  miao2026closing:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Closing the Confidence-Faithfulness Gap in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ruoxi Miao\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Lyle Ungar\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.25052\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Showed correctness direction and verbalized confidence direction are orthogonal (cosine < 0.04) in 7-8B models. Motivates probing internal representations. English-only — our cross-lingual extension is the natural next step.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  xiao2025knowledge:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Analyzing LLMs' Knowledge Boundary Cognition Across Languages Through the Lens of Internal Representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Zheng Xiao\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.13816\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_probing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Closest prior work. Cross-lingual transfer of knowledge-boundary probes (answerable vs unanswerable). Key differences: they probe knowledge boundaries (input-level), we probe correctness (output-dependent); they measure probing accuracy, not ECE/Brier; they test 8 languages, we target 20+.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  civelli2026shared:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Shared Geometry of Difficulty in Multilingual Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Andrea Civelli\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12731\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_probing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer at intermediate layers. Architecture-dependent optimal depth (24-49%). Probes IRT difficulty (question property), not correctness (model property). Critical control for our difficulty ablation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  zhou2025lace:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Zhou\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03136\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"multilingual_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"LACE: adaptive layer ensemble for multilingual calibration. Confirmed 5x ECE gap across 100+ languages. Requires per-language validation data. Our CaCLR needs no non-English correctness labels.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  ravisankar2026dali:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Can you map it to English? The Role of Cross-Lingual Alignment in Multilingual Performance of LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ravisankar\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EACL 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.09378\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_alignment\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"DALI: causal evidence via activation patching that English middle-layer representations fix non-English errors across 24 languages. Strongest causal support for our hypothesis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  miao2026coral:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Correctness-Optimized Residual Activation Lens (CORAL)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ruoxi Miao\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06022\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Transferable correctness probes via regularized MLP on residual activations, ~50% ECE improvement at 53-66% depth. English-only, cross-task. CaCLR positioned as solution to their identified distribution-shift transfer degradation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  joshi2025calibration:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibration Across Layers: Understanding Calibration Evolution in LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Joshi\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Identified low-dimensional calibration direction in residual stream evolving across layers.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  confidence_manifold2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Confidence Manifold: Geometric Structure of Correctness Representations in Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: []\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08159\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Correctness signals occupy 3-8 dimensions, linearly separable. 25 labeled examples achieve 89% of full-data accuracy. All English-only.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  karandikar2021sbece:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Soft Calibration Objectives for Neural Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Karandikar\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2021\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"calibration_methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"SB-ECE: differentiable soft-binned ECE enabling gradient-based calibration optimization. Core component of our CaCLR objective.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  khanmohammadi2025ccps:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibrating LLM Confidence by Probing Perturbed Representation Stability (CCPS)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Khanmohammadi\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.21772\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Calibration via probing perturbed representation stability at final layer. ~55% ECE reduction. English-only, single layer. No cross-lingual or multi-layer analysis.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  liu2025middle:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Middle-Layer Representation Alignment for Cross-Lingual Transfer in Fine-Tuned LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Liu\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Niehues\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"cross_lingual_alignment\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Middle layers form strongest language-agnostic shared space. Supports our hypothesis about intermediate-layer transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  ji2025calibrating:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Calibrating Verbal Uncertainty as a Linear Feature to Reduce Hallucinations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: [\\\\\\\"Ji\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"mechanistic_calibration\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Verbal uncertainty governed by single linear direction in representation space.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ncategories:\\\\n  mechanistic_calibration: \\\\\\\"Probing/steering calibration signals in LLM internal representations\\\\\\\"\\\\n  cross_lingual_probing: \\\\\\\"Cross-lingual transfer of probes/directions in multilingual models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  cross_lingual_alignment: \\\\\\\"Language alignment and shared representations in multilingual LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n  multilingual_calibration: \\\\\\\"Calibration methods for multilingual LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n  calibration_methods: \\\\\\\"General calibration objectives and techniques\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nmeta:\\\\n  created_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-20\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 12\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 6989, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HdvoCpwWqkAhpqTaQVKp96","session_id":"8b4c3866-7c97-4fea-98c8-a02346ba8153","uuid":"15b1cfbb-eda9-4c75-992e-7f14de08e14d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:52:43.698Z"}
